AWS (Amazon Web Services): AWS is a cloud computing platform provided by Amazon that offers IT resources like servers, storage and databases over the internet on a pay as - you - go basis.

Now, cloud services are mainly divided into three types:
1. IAAS- Infrastructure as a service (ex-Amazon EC2)
2. PAAS- Platform as a service (ex- Google app Engine, AWS Elastic Beanstalk etc)
3. SAAS- Software as a service (ex- gmail, FB etc)

AWS, services are core building blocks used to run and secure applications in the cloud:
1. EC2 - Elastic Compute Cloud
2. IAM - Identity and Access Management
3. VPC - Virtual Private Cloud

